 "researcher_notes": "Not in the GEM roster: no row names Malone. It is not the 42-inch Maypearl to Henderson line (P3293) or the Old Ocean Pipeline (P0298). The EIA August 2026 release, sheet Historical Projects (1996-2024) row 515, lists ET Maypearl to Malone: Energy Transfer Co, new pipeline, completed August 2008, Texas, intrastate, 25 miles, 36 inches, 600 MMcf/d, state regulator, no docket number. A NS Energy article repeating an Energy Transfer press release from August 2008 says the 36-inch line runs from systems near Maypearl to the 42-inch line near Malone and adds 600 MCFD out of the Barnett Shale. The two sources trace to the same operator announcement, so they are not independent. The Energy Transfer investor page for the release timed out and was not cited. 25 miles is about 40 km, above the 25 km rule. Owner is the current Energy Transfer LP, which matches the ownership gazetteer exactly. Cost was not found. No Texas Railroad Commission T-4 record was checked. Route not found; no official GIS located. Status operating is inferred from completion in 2008 with no later retirement found."
